{
  "id": "GHSA-xhp5-863h-rhfr",
  "aliases": [],
  "title": "XML-RPC can be used to publish `customize_changeset` posts that bypass checks for `edit_css`",
  "summary": "The generic XML-RPC `wp.newPost` path accepts caller-selected registered post types. A non-Super-Admin site administrator can therefore publish a raw `customize_changeset` post through XML-RPC that contains custom CSS that bypasses the expected check that usually ensures a user can `edit_css`.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.1 has been released containing a fix for the vulnerability, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fix has been backported to all branches back to 4.7.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by Alex Concha of the WordPress Security Team.",
